# `@cloudflare/think` Rules

Use `@cloudflare/think` for the main agent runtime.

The Think agent class should live in:

```txt
src/modules/agent/think-agent.ts
```

Think-specific integration code should live in:

```txt
src/adapters/think/
```

Think tools should be defined in:

```txt
src/modules/agent/agent.tools.ts
```

Think prompts and model-facing text should live in the centralized prompts folder:

```txt
src/prompts/agent.prompts.ts
src/prompts/skill-reflection.prompts.ts
```

Do not put a large system prompt inside `src/index.ts`.

Do not put Slack-specific business logic directly inside the Think agent.

Do not put storage-specific code directly inside Think tools.

Correct:

```txt
Think Agent → Tool → Use Case → Port → Adapter
```

Incorrect:

```txt
Think Agent → Tool → env.DB.prepare(...)
```

Incorrect:

```txt
Think Agent → Tool → fetch("https://slack.com/api/...")
```

Use the installed `@cloudflare/think` package API as the source of truth.

Do not invent undocumented Think APIs.

When unsure about exact Think API names, inspect the installed package types and existing project code before generating implementation.

