# Use Case Rules

Use cases should:

* describe application behavior
* receive typed input
* validate business-level rules
* orchestrate domain logic
* call ports/interfaces
* return typed output or typed result
* be easy to test without Cloudflare runtime
* avoid direct dependency on `env`
* avoid direct dependency on Slack SDKs
* avoid direct dependency on Cloudflare bindings
* avoid direct dependency on a specific storage implementation

Example use case names:

```txt
handleSlackMessage
submitMessageToAgent
summarizeConversation
indexDocument
searchKnowledge
sendSlackReply
runAgentTool
```

Example:

```ts
export class HandleSlackMessageUseCase {
  constructor(
    private readonly thinkSession: ThinkSessionPort,
    private readonly logger: LoggerPort,
  ) {}

  async execute(input: HandleSlackMessageInput): Promise<void> {
    const sessionId = resolveSlackSessionId(input.slack);

    await this.thinkSession.submitUserMessage({
      sessionId,
      text: input.text,
      idempotencyKey: input.idempotencyKey,
      metadata: input.slack,
    });

    this.logger.info("Slack message submitted to Think session", {
      sessionId,
      teamId: input.slack.teamId,
      channelId: input.slack.channelId,
    });
  }
}
```

