# Error Handling

Use typed errors or result objects.

Do not throw raw strings.

Do not leak internal errors to users.

Log useful internal details, but return safe external messages.

For AI/tool failures, return graceful fallbacks.

Preferred:

```ts
throw new AppError("SLACK_EVENT_INVALID", "Slack event payload is invalid");
```

or:

```ts
return err("SLACK_EVENT_INVALID", "Slack event payload is invalid");
```

Use:

```txt
src/shared/errors.ts
src/shared/result.ts
```

---

# Validation

Validate all external input at the boundary.

External input includes:

* Slack events
* HTTP requests
* Worker listener requests
* Think tool inputs
* storage records
* environment values

Do not trust Slack event payloads.

Do not trust tool arguments generated by the model.

Use a validation library when useful.

Keep validation schemas close to the module that owns the input.

---

# Security Rules

* Validate all external input.
* Authenticate requests from the Slack listener to the Worker.
* Verify Slack signatures or Socket Mode source in the listener where applicable.
* Never expose secrets in responses or logs.
* Never hardcode API keys.
* Use Cloudflare secrets and environment bindings where applicable.
* Add rate limiting for public endpoints.
* Treat AI tool calls as untrusted unless explicitly validated.
* Never let the model freely call tools without permission checks and input schema validation.
* Never log full Slack tokens.
* Avoid logging full user messages by default unless explicitly needed and safe for the environment.

---

# Logging Rules

Use `LoggerPort`.

Do not scatter `console.log` everywhere.

Allowed direct console usage:

* local bootstrap
* temporary debugging
* very early startup errors

Preferred:

```ts
logger.info("Slack event received", {
  teamId,
  channelId,
  eventId,
});
```

Never log secrets.

Never log full Slack bot tokens.

---

# Testing Rules

Design use cases so they can be tested without Cloudflare runtime.

Mock ports in tests.

Use in-memory adapters for unit tests.

Do not call real Slack, Cloudflare, D1, KV, R2, Vectorize, Workers AI, or Think runtime in unit tests unless it is an integration test.

Test:

* use cases
* session resolver
* event normalizer
* prompt builders
* tool validation
* adapters where practical
* request validation
* error handling
* idempotency behavior

Preferred tests:

```txt
src/modules/slack/slack-session-resolver.test.ts
src/modules/slack/slack-event-normalizer.test.ts
src/modules/chat/chat.use-case.test.ts
src/modules/agent/agent.tools.test.ts
src/adapters/storage/memory-storage.adapter.test.ts
```

